/** @page mysqlcapabilitiesguide Driver Capabilities

    @tableofcontents

    These capabilities describe what the MySQL driver can do. They are feature flags, not switches
    that enable or disable behavior. Use @ref Qore::SQL::Datasource::getCapabilities() "Datasource::getCapabilities()" to inspect the loaded driver;
    @ref Qore::SQL::Datasource::getCapabilityList() "Datasource::getCapabilityList()" returns readable names for the same flags.
    Transaction and character encoding support require the corresponding client APIs (available with MySQL 5 or later).
    For configurable settings and their accepted values, see @ref mysqloptionsguide.

    |!Feature|!What it means|!Capability flag
    |Transactions|Group changes into a transaction and finish it with @ref Qore::SQL::Datasource::commit() "Datasource::commit()" or undo it with @ref Qore::SQL::Datasource::rollback() "Datasource::rollback()".|@ref Qore::SQL::DBI_CAP_TRANSACTION_MANAGEMENT "DBI_CAP_TRANSACTION_MANAGEMENT"
    |Character encoding|Convert text between Qore strings and the database connection encoding when sending and receiving values.|@ref Qore::SQL::DBI_CAP_CHARSET_SUPPORT "DBI_CAP_CHARSET_SUPPORT"
    |Large text and binary values|Read and bind large text and binary database values as Qore strings and binary values.|@ref Qore::SQL::DBI_CAP_LOB_SUPPORT "DBI_CAP_LOB_SUPPORT"
    |Stored procedures|Execute database procedures through the DBI; procedure syntax and returned values depend on the server. See @ref mysqlstoredprocsguide.|@ref Qore::SQL::DBI_CAP_STORED_PROCEDURES "DBI_CAP_STORED_PROCEDURES"
    |Input parameters|Pass values separately from SQL with \c %v placeholders, so values do not become SQL syntax. See @ref Qore::SQL::Datasource::exec() "Datasource::exec()".|@ref Qore::SQL::DBI_CAP_BIND_BY_VALUE "DBI_CAP_BIND_BY_VALUE"
    |Literal SQL execution|Use @ref Qore::SQL::Datasource::execRaw() "Datasource::execRaw()" to send SQL without Qore placeholder parsing. Values must already be safely represented in the SQL.|@ref Qore::SQL::DBI_CAP_HAS_EXECRAW "DBI_CAP_HAS_EXECRAW"
    |Prepared statements|Prepare SQL once, bind parameters, and fetch results through @ref Qore::SQL::SQLStatement "SQLStatement".|@ref Qore::SQL::DBI_CAP_HAS_STATEMENT "DBI_CAP_HAS_STATEMENT"
    |Single-row queries|Provide a native implementation of @ref Qore::SQL::Datasource::selectRow() "Datasource::selectRow()" for queries expected to return at most one row.|@ref Qore::SQL::DBI_CAP_HAS_SELECT_ROW "DBI_CAP_HAS_SELECT_ROW"
    |Arbitrary-precision numbers|Bind and retrieve decimal values using Qore arbitrary-precision numbers; database precision and configured number conversion still apply.|@ref Qore::SQL::DBI_CAP_HAS_NUMBER_SUPPORT "DBI_CAP_HAS_NUMBER_SUPPORT"
    |Server time zone interpretation|Interpret date/time values using the datasource server time zone. This controls value conversion and does not change the database server configuration.|@ref Qore::SQL::DBI_CAP_SERVER_TIME_ZONE "DBI_CAP_SERVER_TIME_ZONE"
    |Driver options|Read and change supported driver settings with @ref Qore::SQL::Datasource::getOption() "Datasource::getOption()" and @ref Qore::SQL::Datasource::setOption() "Datasource::setOption()". See @ref mysqloptionsguide.|@ref Qore::SQL::DBI_CAP_HAS_OPTION_SUPPORT "DBI_CAP_HAS_OPTION_SUPPORT"
    |Native typed results|Build typed query results directly through @ref Qore::SQL::Datasource::selectTyped() "Datasource::selectTyped()" and @ref Qore::SQL::Datasource::selectRowsTyped() "Datasource::selectRowsTyped()" when built with the corresponding Qore APIs.|@ref Qore::SQL::DBI_CAP_HAS_TYPED_SELECT "DBI_CAP_HAS_TYPED_SELECT"
    |Native columnar results|Return columns suitable for analytical processing through @ref Qore::SQL::Datasource::selectColumnar() "Datasource::selectColumnar()" and @ref Qore::SQL::SQLStatement::fetchColumnar() "SQLStatement::fetchColumnar()" when built with columnar Qore APIs.|@ref Qore::SQL::DBI_CAP_HAS_COLUMNAR_SELECT "DBI_CAP_HAS_COLUMNAR_SELECT"
    |Native bulk loading|Use an optimized database-specific loading path when built with compatible Qore and client APIs. See @ref mysqlnativebulkloadguide for transaction, error handling, and server requirements.|@ref Qore::SQL::DBI_CAP_HAS_BULK_LOAD "DBI_CAP_HAS_BULK_LOAD"

    Native typed and columnar flags indicate optimized driver implementations. When those flags are absent,
    Qore versions providing these APIs can use their compatibility conversion paths; applications should
    check the running Qore version as well as the driver capabilities.

    Statement result metadata is available through @ref Qore::SQL::SQLStatement::describe() "SQLStatement::describe()". This is separate from
    datasource-level @ref Qore::SQL::Datasource::describe() "Datasource::describe()" and its @ref Qore::SQL::DBI_CAP_HAS_DESCRIBE "DBI_CAP_HAS_DESCRIBE" flag.

    @section mysqlcapabilitiescolumnar Columnar Results

    When built against a %Qore library with columnar DBI support, the driver implements
    @ref Qore::SQL::Datasource::selectColumnar() "Datasource::selectColumnar()" and @ref Qore::SQL::SQLStatement::fetchColumnar() "SQLStatement::fetchColumnar()" to return
    @ref Qore::SQL::ColumnarResult "ColumnarResult" objects suitable for DataFrame and analytical workloads.
    Integer and floating-point result columns are returned as dense \c buffer<int64>
    and \c buffer<float64> values. Safe \c DECIMAL(p,s) / \c NUMERIC(p,s) values
    with precision up to 38 are returned as \c buffer<decimal128> when number
    results are not configured as strings.
*/
